WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.134
-Hey guys, last week was crazy.

00:00:02.134 --> 00:00:03.536
Election day should have been
one night,

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:05.338
but it ended up being almost
an entire week.

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:06.906
But anyways,
we wanted to say thank you

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:08.874
to all of the hard-working
journalists and reporters

00:00:08.874 --> 00:00:11.377
who didn't get much sleep
in order to bring us the news.

00:00:11.377 --> 00:00:13.179
Thank you, everyone.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:18.351
Especially Steve Kornacki,
our very own.

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:21.454
Kornacki was up late.
I was getting scared.

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:23.189
At one point he was kind of
falling down.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:25.291
He was just like -- He'd wobble.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.960
I'd be like, "Oh, hold Kornacki.
I can't let him go down.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.562
It's too important.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:30.797
But I did want to say thank you,

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:34.801
so I decided to surprise him
at his office.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:37.870
Man his office is just a mess.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:41.640
He's just downstairs.
He's in our building at MSNBC.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.977
So I just surprised him
this afternoon. Take a look.

00:00:44.977 --> 00:00:46.679
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:50.883
-Okay, here we go.
Gonna find Kornacki.

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:53.086
Is Steve Kornacki there?

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:54.486
We're here.
We are at the right place.

00:00:54.486 --> 00:00:56.722
Look, MSNBC, this is the floor.

00:00:56.722 --> 00:00:58.925
Gosh, it's dark in here.

00:00:58.925 --> 00:01:00.927
Are these temporary offices?

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:02.728
Kornacki?

00:01:02.728 --> 00:01:05.898
Kornacki?
This is like bizarre.

00:01:05.898 --> 00:01:08.435
Steve Kornacki's office.

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:10.670
[ Deep voice ]
Hello, can I come in?

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:14.607
What's up, dude? [ Laughs ]

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:15.474
-How are you doing? Wow!

00:01:15.474 --> 00:01:17.743
-Oh, my.
-This is the office?

00:01:17.743 --> 00:01:20.513
[ Laughter ]
What in the world?

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:21.781
God.
-Welcome to the second floor.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:26.152
-Steve Kornacki, the legend,
the heart throb himself.

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.788
Come on out, buddy.
Steve, you're still standing.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:31.023
You're doing all right.
-I am recharged.

00:01:31.023 --> 00:01:33.293
I'm feeling okay.
-Feeling great?

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:35.227
What happens now to you, though.

00:01:35.227 --> 00:01:36.729
-They put me back into
preservation

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:38.064
for about three
and a half years.

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:39.899
Yeah.
-I got you a little something

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.967
because, you know --
This is for you.

00:01:41.967 --> 00:01:43.569
-Okay. Look at that.

00:01:43.569 --> 00:01:44.870
-Yeah.
-Oh.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:48.240
-It is a Subway $5 gift card
and a bottle of Jack.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.075
We love you.
-This is really kind of you.

00:01:50.075 --> 00:01:51.978
I wish I had something for you.

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:53.646
You're welcome to --
-I don't want anything...

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.148
-There is not much in here.
-...to do with that office.

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:56.316
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:58.852
-Steve Kornacki, everybody!
The one and only.

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:01.487 line:0%
Good job, buddy. Fist bump.
-Alright. Thanks for visiting.

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:03.022 line:0%
-Yeah, no problem.
We'll be back with more

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:05.725 line:0%
"Tonight Show," everybody.
Come on back.

